{"url": "https://phdneuroscience.unibe.ch/application_and_admission/index_eng.html", "final_url": "https://phdneuroscience.unibe.ch/application_and_admission/index_eng.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-29", "text": "Application and Admission - Specialized PhD in Neuroscience / BENEFRI\nHomepage\nMenu\nInhalt\nKontakt\nSuche\nSprachwahl\nWichtige Seiten\nSpecialized PhD in Neuroscience / BENEFRI\nMenu \u00f6ffnen\nMenu schliessen\nSpecialized PhD in Neuroscience / BENEFRI\nApplication and Admission\nHomepage\nPhD Program\nApplication and Admission\nActivities\nAbout us\nPortal\nUniBE\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nApplication and Admission\nAdmission to the program is granted at the request of the doctoral student (UniBE or UniFR) by the Program Committee of the Specialized Neuroscience Program consisting of two representatives from the Universities of Bern and Fribourg without any additional evaluation or selection of the doctoral students or their projects. The program is opened to students with background in Neuroscience including Neurology, Psychiatry, Physiology, Anatomy, Biology, Bioengineering, Biomedical sciences, Neuropsychology. Students from other Universities that wish to join the program can send a request to the Program Committee.\nRegistration Form\n(WORD, 2.4 MB)\nUniBE students\nPlease send this form to:\nProf. Dr. Antoine Adamantidis (antoine.adamantidis@unibe.ch),\nAss. Prof. Dr. St\u00e9phane Ciocchi (stephane.ciocchi@unibe.ch) and\nTr\u00e2n Vu (tran.vu@unibe.ch)\nUniFR students:\nPlease send this form to:\nProf. Dr. Gregor Rainer (gregor.rainer@unifr.ch) and\nTr\u00e2n Vu (tran.vu@unibe.ch)\nShare\nFacebook\nE-Mail\nLinkedIn\nPrint\nYou are here\nSpecialized PhD in Neuroscience / BENEFRI\nApplication and Admission\nTop\nWeitere Informationen \u00fcber diesen Webauftritt\nPortal Universit\u00e4t Bern\nSprachwahl\nEN\nSite-Suche\nSearch\nSearch\nRechtliches und Impressum\n\u00a9 2026\nUniversity of Bern,\nHochschulstrasse 6,\nC